 - `scripts/full/train_chronos2_stage1.sh` and `scripts/full/train_chronos2_stage2.sh`
 - `scripts/full/train_zeus_stage1.sh` and `scripts/full/train_zeus_stage2.sh`
 
+The metadata helper can also be added to custom grid scripts. Call it immediately after a successful DeepSpeed
+command, using the same output and backbone variables:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/full/save_ts_encoder_config.py "$STAGE1_OUT" \
+  --encoder-type timesfm2_5 \
+  --backbone-path "$TIMESFM_MODEL_PATH"
+```
+
+Supported encoder types are `native`, `timesfm2_5`, `chronos2`, and `zeus`. For external encoders the helper
+writes `ts_encoder_type`, the backbone path, hidden width, and `ts.patch_size`; for Zeus it also writes
